WEBVTT

00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:44.211
(wings fluttering)

00:00:44.294 --> 00:00:46.171
(birds chirping)

00:00:50.175 --> 00:00:51.885
(airplane engine rumbling)

00:01:01.436 --> 00:01:03.480
All right, that's it.
好了，就这样

00:01:03.564 --> 00:01:06.483
(men grunting with effort)
好了，就这样

00:01:06.567 --> 00:01:09.152
One, two, three.
1，2，3

00:01:10.612 --> 00:01:12.531
(bicycle bell rings)
片名：纳尼亚传奇：黎明踏浪号

00:01:21.248 --> 00:01:23.250
(low, indistinct conversation)
（祖国母亲需要你
应征入伍报名处）

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:28.046
Are you sure you're 18?
你真的18岁？

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:29.590
Why? Do I look older?
怎么，难道不像吗？

00:01:37.973 --> 00:01:39.516
Alberta Scrubb?
艾伯塔·斯克拉布？

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:40.809
That's a typographical error.
印刷错误，中间少了个字母

00:01:40.893 --> 00:01:43.478
It's supposed to be Albert A. Scrubb.
印刷错误，中间少了个字母

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:47.232
Edmund, you're supposed to be
helping me with the groceries.
我们该去买日用品了

00:01:47.316 --> 00:01:48.609
(chuckling)
我们该去买日用品了

00:01:52.487 --> 00:01:53.947
Better luck next time, eh, squirt?
下次祝你好运，小家伙？

00:02:00.495 --> 00:02:02.039
Squirt?
小家伙

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:04.499
He barely had two years on me.
他不过才比我大两岁

00:02:04.583 --> 00:02:05.876
I'm a king.
我可是国王，身经百战
统帅过千军万马

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:09.296
I've fought wars, and...
and I've led armies.
我可是国王，身经百战
统帅过千军万马

00:02:09.379 --> 00:02:10.797
Not in this world.
那是另一个世界

00:02:10.881 --> 00:02:14.009
Yeah. Instead, I'm stuck here doing battle
是的，可是在这个世界
我只有…

00:02:14.092 --> 00:02:16.470
with Eustace Clarence Scrubb.
和尤斯塔斯·克拉伦斯·斯克拉布打架的份儿

00:02:16.553 --> 00:02:18.764
If anyone so deserved a name.
一想起来就觉着丢人

00:02:21.433 --> 00:02:22.684
What are you doing?
你干什么呢？

00:02:23.644 --> 00:02:24.645
Nothing.
没什么

00:02:25.646 --> 00:02:27.147
Come on, then.
我们走吧

00:02:33.779 --> 00:02:37.658
EUSTACE:
Dear diary, it is now day 253
亲爱的日记
该死的表哥埃德蒙

00:02:37.741 --> 00:02:41.245
since my wretched cousins
Edmund and Lucy invaded our house.
和表姐露西闯进我家已经253天了

00:02:41.328 --> 00:02:43.539
I'm not sure how much longer
I can cope living with them,
不知道还要和他们一起呆多久

00:02:43.622 --> 00:02:45.082
having to share my things.
真是度日如年

00:02:45.958 --> 00:02:49.753
If only one could treat relatives
like one treats insects,
要是对待亲戚能像对待小猫小狗一样

00:02:49.837 --> 00:02:51.672
all my problems would be solved.
那就太好了

00:02:51.755 --> 00:02:55.384
I could simply put them in a jar
or pin them to my wall.
我会把他们关起来，或是臭揍一顿

00:02:55.467 --> 00:02:56.760
LUCY: I'm home.
我回来了，你好

00:02:57.469 --> 00:02:58.971
Hello!
我回来了，你好

00:02:59.054 --> 00:03:04.351
Note to self: investigate legal
ramifications of impaling relatives.
自我提示
调研一下让亲戚消失

00:03:05.352 --> 00:03:06.436
(door closes)

00:03:08.313 --> 00:03:10.315
MAN (on radio): That concludes
the war news from the Western Front.

00:03:10.399 --> 00:03:12.484
Hello, Uncle Harold.
I tried to find some carrots,
你好，哈罗德舅舅
我想买些胡萝卜

00:03:12.568 --> 00:03:14.570
but all they had were turnips again.
可是市场上只有大头菜

00:03:14.653 --> 00:03:16.488
Shall I start making soup?
我可以开始做汤了吗？

00:03:16.572 --> 00:03:18.657
Aunt Alberta's on her way home.
艾伯塔舅妈快到家了

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:20.325
(coughing)
艾伯塔舅妈快到家了

00:03:21.368 --> 00:03:22.786
Uncle Harold.
哈罗德舅舅？

00:03:23.704 --> 00:03:25.497
EUSTACE: Father!
爸爸，埃德蒙朝你做鬼脸

00:03:25.581 --> 00:03:27.374
Edmund's making faces at you.
爸爸，埃德蒙朝你做鬼脸

00:03:27.457 --> 00:03:30.169
-(spits)
-Why, you little...
你这小…

00:03:30.252 --> 00:03:32.880
-Father, he's gonna hit me.
-LUCY: Edmund, look.
爸爸，他要打我

00:03:33.338 --> 00:03:34.715
It's from Susan.
苏珊来信了

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:37.301
SUSAN: I do wish
you were here with us.
我真希望咱们能在一起

00:03:37.384 --> 00:03:40.804
It's been such an adventure,
but nothing like our times in Narnia.
来美国一路很危险
不过比在纳尼亚时差远了

00:03:42.014 --> 00:03:45.767
America is very exciting,
except we never see Father.
美国非常刺激

00:03:45.851 --> 00:03:48.562
He works so very hard.
I was invited...
可惜还没有见到爸爸，他一直忙得要命

00:03:48.645 --> 00:03:51.982
"To the British consul's tea party
this week by a naval officer,
本周去参加英国领事馆的茶会

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:53.984
who happens to be very handsome.
那军官长得非常帅

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:57.029
I think he fancies me." Hmm.
我想他是迷上我了

00:03:57.112 --> 00:04:00.282
"It seems the Germans have made
the crossing difficult right now.
由于德国封锁
目前穿越大西洋非常困难

00:04:00.365 --> 00:04:01.617
Times are hard.
时局很艰难

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:05.078
Mother hopes you both won't mind
another few months in Cambridge."
妈妈希望你们俩能在剑桥再坚持几个月

00:04:06.288 --> 00:04:09.333
Another few months?
How will we survive?
让我们怎么坚持？

00:04:09.416 --> 00:04:11.126
You're lucky.
你很幸运了

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:14.630
At least you've got your own room.
I'm stuck with mullet mouth.
至少有自己的房间
我还得跟那小子一起住

00:04:14.713 --> 00:04:17.257
Susan and Peter are the lucky ones.
真正幸运的是彼得和苏珊

00:04:17.883 --> 00:04:19.092
Off on adventures.
可以去外面冒险

00:04:19.176 --> 00:04:21.678
Yeah, they're the eldest,
and we're the youngest.
是呀，就因为他们大，我们小

00:04:22.513 --> 00:04:23.889
We don't matter as much.
老天爷真是太不公平了

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:27.142
Do you think I look anything like Susan?
你说我有没有像苏珊的地方？

00:04:27.226 --> 00:04:29.102
(sighs)

00:04:29.186 --> 00:04:32.648
Lucy, have you seen this ship before?
你以前见过这种船吗？

00:04:32.731 --> 00:04:34.358
Yes.
见过，有点像纳尼亚的风格，对吗？

00:04:34.441 --> 00:04:36.360
It's very Narnian-looking, isn't it?
见过，有点像纳尼亚的风格，对吗？

00:04:36.985 --> 00:04:38.237
Yeah.
没错

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:41.073
Well, just another reminder
that we're here and not there.
这正好说明我们现在不是在纳尼亚

00:04:41.156 --> 00:04:45.118
There once were two orphans,
who wasted their time
从前有两个傻瓜，吃饱了没事可干

00:04:45.202 --> 00:04:47.120
believing in Narnian nursery rhymes.
整天就知道纳尼亚、纳尼亚的

00:04:47.204 --> 00:04:48.956
-Please let me hit him.
-No!
-你别拦着我
-不行

00:04:49.039 --> 00:04:51.083
-Don't you ever knock?
-It's my house.
-你不会敲门吗？
-这是我家，我敲不着

00:04:51.166 --> 00:04:53.293
I'll do as I please.
You're just guests.
-你不会敲门吗？
-这是我家，我敲不着

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:56.922
What's so fascinating
about that picture anyway?
那幅画有什么可大惊小怪的？

00:04:57.881 --> 00:04:58.924
It's hideous.
无聊透顶

00:04:59.007 --> 00:05:00.634
You won't see it from
the other side of the door.
嫌无聊你出去好了

00:05:01.718 --> 00:05:04.054
Edmund, it looks like the
water's actually moving.
埃德蒙，画里的水好像在动

00:05:04.847 --> 00:05:07.432
What rubbish. See?
That's what happens when you read
我看你就是…

00:05:07.516 --> 00:05:09.852
all those fanciful novels
and fairy tales of yours.
听多了童话故事鬼迷心窍了

00:05:09.935 --> 00:05:11.979
There once was a boy called Eustace,
从前有个男孩名叫尤斯塔斯

00:05:12.062 --> 00:05:14.690
who read books full of facts
that were useless.
他只知道看那些空洞无物的现代故事

00:05:14.773 --> 00:05:17.359
People who read fairy tales
are always the sort
那些痴迷虚幻故事的人

00:05:17.442 --> 00:05:19.820
who become a hideous burden
to people like me,
对于像我这样
时刻关注现实的人而言

00:05:19.903 --> 00:05:21.822
who read books of real information.
只是一种可怕的负担…

00:05:21.905 --> 00:05:23.031
Hideous burden?!
可怕的负担？

00:05:24.032 --> 00:05:26.827
I haven't seen you lift a finger since
we've been here.
我看你才是真正的最可怕的负担

00:05:28.287 --> 00:05:29.663
I have a right mind to tell your father
我早该告诉舅舅
是你偷吃了艾伯塔舅妈的糖果

00:05:29.746 --> 00:05:31.248
it was you who stole
Aunt Alberta's sweets.
我早该告诉舅舅
是你偷吃了艾伯塔舅妈的糖果

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:32.833
-EUSTACE: Liar.
-EDMUND: Oh, really?
-你胡说
-是吗？

00:05:32.916 --> 00:05:34.585
Edmund, the painting.
埃德蒙，你看那画

00:05:34.668 --> 00:05:36.378
EDMUND: I found them under your bed,
我在你床底下发现的，知道吗？

00:05:36.461 --> 00:05:38.881
and you know what?
I licked every one of them.
我在你床底下发现的，知道吗？

00:05:38.964 --> 00:05:41.717
EUSTACE: Ooh! I'm infected!
With you!
你会把疾病传染给我的

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:43.010
(gasps)
你会把疾病传染给我的

00:05:45.804 --> 00:05:47.514
What's going on here?
这是怎么回事？

00:05:47.598 --> 00:05:49.766
-EDMUND: Lucy, do you think--
-EUSTACE: It's some kind of trick.
-露西，你觉得…
-这里一定有鬼

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:51.351
Stop it or I'll tell mother.
停下，不然我告诉妈妈

00:05:51.435 --> 00:05:54.188
Mother! Mother!
妈妈

00:05:56.690 --> 00:05:58.275
I'll just smash the rotten thing.
看我把这破画给砸了

00:05:58.358 --> 00:05:59.610
No, Eustace!
不，尤斯塔斯，不

00:05:59.693 --> 00:06:02.196
-No! No! No!
-Eustace, please stop it.
不，尤斯塔斯，不

00:06:02.279 --> 00:06:04.281
-Get off me! Get off!
-LUCY: Let go of it, Eustace!
别管我，走开

00:06:04.364 --> 00:06:07.492
Put it down! Let go!
-放下
-放下

00:06:10.078 --> 00:06:11.830
-(grunting)
-(Lucy screams)

00:06:14.583 --> 00:06:16.710
(gasps)

00:06:22.758 --> 00:06:24.301
(muffled groaning)

00:06:32.976 --> 00:06:34.895
(gasps)

00:06:34.978 --> 00:06:37.439
-Edmund!
-(gasps)
埃德蒙

00:06:37.523 --> 00:06:39.149
Aah! What's happening?
What's happening?
埃德蒙

00:06:39.233 --> 00:06:40.692
(deep rumbling, creaking)
怎么回事？

00:06:40.776 --> 00:06:42.110
EUSTACE:
Where are we?
这是哪儿？

00:06:44.488 --> 00:06:45.822
Eustace, swim!
尤斯塔斯，快点游

00:06:45.906 --> 00:06:47.491
EUSTACE: What's going on?
怎么回事？

00:06:47.574 --> 00:06:49.409
LUCY: Eustace, come on!
尤斯塔斯，快游

00:06:49.493 --> 00:06:50.994
EDMUND: Come on, move!
快，快游

00:06:51.078 --> 00:06:53.247
LUCY: Keep swimming!
不要停下

00:06:55.374 --> 00:06:56.583
EUSTACE: Edmund!
埃德蒙

00:07:01.755 --> 00:07:04.216
It's all right. I've got you.
好了，我抓到你了

00:07:05.509 --> 00:07:06.718
Caspian!
凯斯宾

00:07:06.802 --> 00:07:09.555
-Lucy.
-Edmund, it's Caspian!
露西

00:07:09.638 --> 00:07:12.558
It's all right, boys. You're safe now.
没事了，孩子们，你们安全了

00:07:12.641 --> 00:07:15.269
-EDMUND: We in Narnia?
-CASPIAN: Yes, you're in Narnia.
是的，这是纳尼亚

00:07:15.352 --> 00:07:17.062
I don't want to go!
我不想来这儿

00:07:17.145 --> 00:07:19.064
I want to go back to England!
我想回英国，我要回英国去

00:07:19.147 --> 00:07:21.191
I'm going back to England!
我想回英国，我要回英国去

00:07:21.275 --> 00:07:22.693
Hold on.
抓紧

